  "goal": "Surpass the source-paper result on the same task: Select and recover an original source performance branch: information recovered by a population decoder from held-out CA1 responses (Figure 2C), or estimator accuracy against source-defined known truth in the original simulations. Do not optimize the descriptive direct-pair MI value. These source branches remain distinct and no scalar mixture or new endpoint is selected here.",
  "primary_outputs": [
    "Candidate method and outputs for the source task: Select and recover an original source performance branch: information recovered by a population decoder from held-out CA1 responses (Figure 2C), or estimator accuracy against source-defined known truth in the original simulations. Do not optimize the descriptive direct-pair MI value. These source branches remain distinct and no scalar mixture or new endpoint is selected here.",
    "Source-paper comparison for Original source held-out population-decoder information or known-truth estimator error; branch and exact baseline unresolved: The source population branch computes information in the held-out SVM confusion matrix, I(S;S_hat) in bits; this lower bound is distinct from direct empirical pair MI. A source simulation accuracy branch needs its original known-truth target and error definition. Recover a single branch-specific ordered metric and numeric author comparator rather than treating larger direct MI as accuracy."
  ],
  "success_criteria": [
